// The -1/-1 counter ([CR#122.1a]): each subtracts 1 from power and toughness
// in layer 7c ([CR#613.4c]), conferred directly as the ability-free `Property`
// flavor. The conferral is what ONE counter confers; the model applies it once
// per counter held, so it reads no count.
//
// STOP (semantics-v2-definition-bodies). The annihilation rule ([CR#704.5q])
// is not written here. It removes "N +1/+1 and N -1/-1 counters … where N is
// the smaller of" the two counts, and `Amount` has no minimum of two amounts
// (`ArithOp` is plus/minus/times/differenceBetween). It is also a `SbaRule`
// rather than a conferral: [CR#704.5q] scopes a permanent that has BOTH kinds,
// which is a predicate over the permanent, not a property of one counter.
// Routed to `semantics-v2-counter-annihilation-sba`.
CounterKind(
    name: "m1m1Counter",
    params: [],
    compound_stem: Measure,
    compound_onset: Consonant,
    spelling: "-1/-1",
    holder: Object,
    confers: [boost(down(1), down(1))],
)
